# `todo/t0972` — matching a CALL RESULT never drops the moved-out payload;
# matching the same value through a LOCAL does.
#
# ⭐ THE WHOLE DEFECT IS ONE TOKEN. `match make_ok():` leaks; hoisting to
# `Result[T, String] r = make_ok()` and writing `match r:` is ASan-CLEAN. Same
# function, same payload, same arms.
#
# ⚠⚠ BOTH HALVES OF THAT DISCRIMINATOR ARE CELLS BELOW, NOT PROSE. The two
# CLEAN local-scrutinee forms are what make the axis provable: without them a
# future fix could free the call-result binding while REGRESSING the local form
# and this fixture would still go green (Core #12 — the control is what makes
# the claim checkable). They contribute no leak records today, so the fixture's
# RED is exactly the two call-result cells.
#
# ⚠⚠ THE NAME SAYS `payload`, NOT `callable`, AND THAT IS A CORRECTION. This was
# filed as a `Callable`-specific defect on the strength of a `String` control
# that read CLEAN. That control was WRONG: it used a short String literal, which
# never leaves the small-string buffer and allocates nothing. With a heap-forced
# String — a 42-character VALUE, built as a 41-character literal plus a
# runtime-concatenated digit so it cannot sit in the buffer — the twin leaks
# 43 bytes (42 + NUL) in 1 allocation on C AND LLVM, while the LOCAL-scrutinee
# twin of THAT is clean. So the axis is CALL-RESULT-vs-LOCAL and the defect is
# general. Both payload types are cells below, so the fixture cannot drift back
# to the narrower claim.
#
# MECHANISM, read off the emitted C. Both scrutinee forms emit the enum's drop
# fn. In the arm the payload is COPIED OUT into the binding and the enum's slot
# is `memset` to zero, so the drop then frees a zeroed slot:
#   __s5 = *(GorgetClosure *)(__v48);            // move out
#   memset(__v15, 0, sizeof(GorgetClosure));     // slot zeroed
#   ...
#   Result__…__drop(&__s2);                      // frees nothing
# The LOCAL-scrutinee form additionally emits a free for the moved-out BINDING —
# where the value actually lives after the arm runs — and the CALL-RESULT form
# does not.
#
# ⚠ NOT the materialization class (`todo/t0937`, closed): every cell prints the
# CORRECT value on both backends.
#
# INTENDED: prints 2, the 42-character string, then 3 and the string again from
# the two local-scrutinee controls — and is ASan-clean.
String mk(int n):
    String s = "abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789ABCD_"
    return s + f"{n}"

Result[Callable[int(int)], String] make_callable():
    return Ok((int x): x + 1)

Result[String, String] make_string():
    return Ok(mk(1))

Result[Callable[int(int)], String] make_callable2():
    return Ok((int x): x + 2)

Result[String, String] make_string2():
    return Ok(mk(2))

void main():
    # ---- THE DEFECT: the scrutinee is a CALL RESULT. Both cells leak. -----
    match make_callable():
        case Ok(h):
            print(h(1))                     # 2
        case Error(msg):
            print(msg)

    match make_string():
        case Ok(s):
            print(s)                        # …ABCD_1
        case Error(msg2):
            print(msg2)

    # ---- THE CONTROL: the same values through a LOCAL. Both CLEAN. --------
    # One token apart from the cells above, and that token is the whole axis.
    Result[Callable[int(int)], String] rc = make_callable2()
    match rc:
        case Ok(h2):
            print(h2(1))                    # 3
        case Error(msg3):
            print(msg3)

    Result[String, String] rs = make_string2()
    match rs:
        case Ok(s2):
            print(s2)                       # …ABCD_2
        case Error(msg4):
            print(msg4)
